WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.936
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.771
Thank you for watching.
I appreciate it.

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:07.140
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.042
♪♪

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.010
Former president Trump
is in the news.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:14.380
Apparently he's been trashing
Florida governor Ron DeSantis

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.017 line:0%
behind his back, calling him
a dull guy who has no chance of

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:20.553 line:0%
beating him in a potential
2024 matchup.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:22.421 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.421 --> 00:00:25.058
Trump was like, "I have to
insult him behind his back

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.260
'cause I can't tweet it
to his face."

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.028
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.562
I feel like Trump is slipping.

00:00:30.562 --> 00:00:32.298
A few years ago, he would have
had like 10 nicknames

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:35.502
for this guy by now.
It's like, "Ron Dull-Santis."

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:37.103
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:40.139
I think the insults backfired
'cause just hearing Trump's name

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:43.109
jump-started Biden's approval
rating back up in the 50s.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.745
[ Laughter ]
It's in the 50s now. Yeah.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.613
I think this is
actually a nice change

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:49.582
'cause usually when two Florida
guys get into a fight,

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:50.917
they're drunk and shirtless.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.452
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.687
But DeSantis doesn't seem fazed.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.355
He said that he's going to
handle the insult

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:58.324
just like COVID
and completely ignore it.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:01.227
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.963
And speaking of
the former president,

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:06.733
this weekend he held
his first rally of the year.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.901
Let's take a listen
to what he had to say.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:12.138
-The grocery shelves,
the department-store shelves,

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:13.806
they're empty.

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:16.275
You had an excuse
not to buy Christmas gifts.

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:18.178
You say to your loved one,
"Darling, I'm sorry.

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.546
I love you very much,
but I just can't.

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:23.048
There's no merchandise
in Tiffany.

00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:25.217
I wanted to buy you
the most beautiful ring,

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:26.986
but they don't have any rings
anymore.

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.988
Nobody has anything.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.724
We never even heard the term
"supply change."

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:36.328
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.328 --> 00:01:38.832
-Supply change.

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:41.201
Well, a year off,
and he's still got it.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:44.136
I think he's still got it.
I think...

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:47.107
[ Cheers and applause ]
I think he's still got it.

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:50.076
He's right. He's right.
He's right.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:52.077
We've never heard the term
"supply change."

00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:54.079
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:55.915
-And then he started talking
about things

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.717
being expensive
'cause of inflammation.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:01.921
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.891
Trump knows exactly what
concerns working families --

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.759
the ring inventory at Tiffany's.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:10.363
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.765
Well, guys, as if we're not
dealing with enough right now,

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:16.035 line:0%
doctors are warning people
against a new TikTok trend

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:19.105 line:0%
called "sleepy chicken,"

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:21.707 line:0%
where people cook chicken
in NyQuil.

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:22.875
-No!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:24.710
-Yes.
-No.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:27.647
-Yeah.
-What?

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:29.014
-There's actually another name

00:02:29.014 --> 00:02:30.316
for chicken
that makes you sleepy.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.484
It's called turkey.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:34.386
Just eat turkey.

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:36.155
That's right.
Doctors are warning people

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:38.558
against cooking chicken
in cold medicine.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.326
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.295
I mean, the recipe is wild.
Take a look at this recipe.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:45.698
It says add oil to pan
then add chicken.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:48.034
Then sauté in bottle of NyQuil.

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.301
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:50.970
After that,
cook chicken through,

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.373
transfer to plate,
and then enjoy.

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:56.943
After that, wake up facedown
in plate four hours later.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.277
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.277 --> 00:03:00.146
Next, stumble into garage,

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:02.614
drive car straight through
garage door.

00:03:02.614 --> 00:03:05.618
Then drive to Taco Bell
on wrong side of road

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.520
going three miles per hour.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:12.091
After that, remove shirt, demand
eggplant parm and a Twinkie.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.560 line:0%
Then get arrested.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:17.329
Next, use one phone call on
the only number you remember --

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:18.598
the house you grew up
in as a kid.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:19.965
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:24.303
Then spend night in jail,
join gang for protection.

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:27.140
After that, get neck tattoo of
prison nickname --

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.340
"Sizzurp Chicken."

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:34.179
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:34.179 --> 00:03:38.551 line:0%
Then gain freedom but lose job
as high school principal.

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.819 line:0%
And finally,
refrigerate leftovers.

00:03:40.819 --> 00:03:43.122 line:0%
So, I mean,
it's a tricky recipe.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.925
Just stay away from it.
[ Applause ]

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.493
Hey, did you guys see this?

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:50.529 line:0%
A Norwegian cruise ship
canceled its trip

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:52.632 line:0%
mid-voyage due to COVID.

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:53.833 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:57.270 line:0%
And now a bunch of passengers
are stuck at sea.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.806
Norwegian told the passengers,
"There's no reason to panic.

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:01.541
There's plenty of NyQuil chicken
for everyone."

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:03.509
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:05.311
Passengers are furious.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.779
They're like,
"When I booked this cruise

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.881
during a COVID surge,
who knew this could happen?"

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:13.118
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.118 --> 00:04:14.720
Everyone's just stranded
and angry.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.288
That's got to be
a lot of pressure

00:04:16.288 --> 00:04:17.823
for the cruise-ship comic.

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:20.593
"So, where are you folks
being held from?"

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:23.095
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:25.831
I saw that over the weekend
on the Saturday edition

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:28.534
of the "Today" show,
one meteorologist had a cough

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.537
coming on, and she did her best
to fight through it.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.039
Just watch this.

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:35.841
-Well, our friends out west have
lucked out with dry conditions

00:04:35.841 --> 00:04:37.743
and mild conditions out towards
the Rockies.

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:40.513
And, of course, we're seeing...
that winter storm

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.981
that's going to impact
the East Coast.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:45.317
[ Coughs ]
Excuse me.

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:47.887
Let's go ahead and take a look
at your...forecast.

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:50.756
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:52.158
-Somara getting
a little bit of water,

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:54.260
and she will be back with more
in just a bit.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.594
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:56.629
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:59.165
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.167
-Oh, poor thing.

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.735
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.735 --> 00:05:06.139
-She sounds like the captain of
a Norwegian cruise.

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:08.006
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.006 --> 00:05:11.277
At first it looked like she was
just overcome with the emotion

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:12.979
at the sight of a cold front.

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:17.049
And then "I -- I promised myself
I wouldn't do this."

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:19.118
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:21.087
Could we just watch that again
just 'cause it's funny?

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.288
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:24.890
-Of course, we're seeing...
that winter storm

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:26.459
that's going to impact
the East Coast.

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:29.461
[ Coughs ]
Excuse me.

00:05:29.461 --> 00:05:31.964
Let's go ahead and take a look
at your...forecast.

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:34.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:44.176
-Some business news --
I saw that once again

00:05:44.176 --> 00:05:47.146 line:0%
Netflix increased its monthly
subscription prices.

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:50.683 line:0%
[ Audience booing ]

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:53.619
Apparently Netflix's plan is
to take so much of our money

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:55.822
that we'll have to enter
a real-life squid game.

00:05:55.822 --> 00:05:57.222
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.222 --> 00:05:59.525
Netflix says that you can
either pay the increase

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:01.727
or enjoy not knowing
what anyone's talking about

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:02.895
for the next 70 years.

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:04.229
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.229 --> 00:06:06.031
And finally, I heard that
there's a new push here

00:06:06.031 --> 00:06:09.068
in New York City to put
trash containers on the streets

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:10.369
so that there aren't
giant mountains

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:13.172
of trash bags on the sidewalks.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:15.541
It's like a developer came
in and said, "I got it --

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:16.776
rat condominiums."

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:19.111
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:20.546
It should be great.

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:22.881
This way, instead of having to
look at ugly piles of trash,

00:06:22.881 --> 00:06:26.685
we'll get to see all
these beautiful dumpsters.

00:06:26.685 --> 00:06:28.554
Well, guys, as the country

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:30.322
continues to deal
with the pandemic,

00:06:30.322 --> 00:06:33.059 line:0%
the director of the CDC
just said that she's aiming

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:36.228 line:0%
to improve the agency's
COVID messaging.

00:06:36.228 --> 00:06:37.830 line:0%
Yeah, then
in her next interview,

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:41.167
she said the CDC is not aiming
to improve their messaging.

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:43.402
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:45.938
Yeah, in the CDC's defense,
it's hard to get any message out

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:50.175
when every ad on TV
is for Caesars Sportsbook.

00:06:50.175 --> 00:06:52.644
Yep, the CDC wants
to communicate more clearly,

00:06:52.644 --> 00:06:54.747
so going forward,
their press releases

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:57.016
will no longer be
in the Wingdings font.

00:07:02.655 --> 00:07:05.290 line:0%
Some more news.
I read that Neil Gorsuch

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:07.159 line:0%
is the only
Supreme Court justice

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:10.162 line:0%
who won't wear a mask
to help protect his colleague,

00:07:10.162 --> 00:07:12.831 line:0%
Sonia Sotomayor,
who has diabetes.

00:07:12.831 --> 00:07:15.701
[ Audience boos ]

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:17.202
You know Gorsuch is the guy

00:07:17.202 --> 00:07:19.172
who touches every bagel
before picking one.

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:21.840
You know that? He's like...

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:24.143
You guys remember Neil Gorsuch.

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:27.046
He used to work
for the law firm

00:07:27.046 --> 00:07:29.081
Rogan, Hogan &amp; Facebook.

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:31.517
Hey, I saw a news anchor
in Mexico who looked like

00:07:31.517 --> 00:07:33.252
he finally hit
his breaking point

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:34.953
with people
who won't get vaccinated.

00:07:34.953 --> 00:07:36.188
Check this out.

00:07:36.188 --> 00:07:38.557 line:0%
-iUstedes! [Bleep]

00:07:38.557 --> 00:07:42.228 line:0%
[ Shouting Spanish ]

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:44.296 line:0%
[Bleep]

00:07:44.296 --> 00:07:46.165 line:0%
[ Shouting Spanish ]

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:47.733 line:0%
[Bleep]

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:49.735 line:0%
[ Shouting Spanish ]

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:00.413 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:00.413 --> 00:08:02.381
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:04.650
♪♪

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.385
-Yo!

00:08:06.385 --> 00:08:09.622
You know that's how Dr. Fauci
feels on the inside.

00:08:09.622 --> 00:08:11.990
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:14.794
Hey, I heard that today
former New York City mayor

00:08:14.794 --> 00:08:16.929 line:0%
Bill de Blasio announced
that he is not running

00:08:16.929 --> 00:08:19.598 line:0%
for Governor of New York.
He then --

00:08:19.598 --> 00:08:21.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:21.968 --> 00:08:24.703
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.703 --> 00:08:27.840
He then waited over ten minutes
for someone to say, "Aw."

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:29.208
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:30.943
Yep, de Blasio
won't run for governor.

00:08:30.943 --> 00:08:32.878
He said he wants
to spend more time at home

00:08:32.878 --> 00:08:36.115
being booed by his family.

00:08:36.115 --> 00:08:37.449
Did he really
have to announce that?

00:08:37.449 --> 00:08:39.318
I mean, he might as well
have announced that he won't be

00:08:39.318 --> 00:08:41.254
performing at the Super Bowl
Halftime Show.

00:08:41.254 --> 00:08:42.721
It's like, "Yeah, we know."

00:08:42.721 --> 00:08:44.924 line:0%
Some business news here.
Apparently airlines

00:08:44.924 --> 00:08:47.092 line:0%
are dealing with
the ongoing pilot shortage

00:08:47.092 --> 00:08:50.930 line:0%
by raising pay
and lowering the requirements.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:52.464 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:08:52.464 --> 00:08:55.568
Passengers said, "That's nice."
And, "Wait. What?"

00:08:55.568 --> 00:08:57.537
[ Laughter ]

00:08:57.537 --> 00:08:59.271
This probably explains
why my last pilot

00:08:59.271 --> 00:09:00.873
was wearing a Petsmart uniform.

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:02.808
[ Laughter ]

00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:05.578
Yeah, it's not very reassuring
when your pilot is the same guy

00:09:05.578 --> 00:09:07.612
who drove your Uber
to the airport.

00:09:07.612 --> 00:09:09.882
He's like, "Alright. Let's go.
Here we go. Come on."

00:09:09.882 --> 00:09:12.618
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.618 --> 00:09:15.221
Now instead of needing
years of experience, pilots just

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:18.724
have to complete a CAPTCHA
that proves that they're human.

00:09:18.724 --> 00:09:20.526
Yeah, they'll hire anyone
right now.

00:09:20.526 --> 00:09:22.861
Here's the newest United pilot
I saw.

00:09:22.861 --> 00:09:27.666 line:0%
-[ Shouting Spanish ]

00:09:27.666 --> 00:09:30.002 line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:09:30.002 --> 00:09:33.171
-That's a bit much.
-Geez.

00:09:33.171 --> 00:09:36.241
-Well, speaking of flying,
a man went viral on TikTok

00:09:36.241 --> 00:09:39.211
when he shared his experience
as the only passenger

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:42.481
on an eight-hour
international flight.

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:44.750
Somehow we have a pilot
and passenger shortage.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.184
I don't know.

00:09:46.184 --> 00:09:49.322
Of course, they wouldn't let him
board until his zone was called.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:52.992
"Group two."

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:57.163
"Sorry, sir.

00:09:57.163 --> 00:10:00.699
You're group four.

00:10:00.699 --> 00:10:03.903
Group two. One more time."

00:10:03.903 --> 00:10:05.904
It's weird
when the pilot's like,

00:10:05.904 --> 00:10:09.174
"Uh, we will now be making
our approach, Tom."

00:10:09.174 --> 00:10:11.010
Hey, this is also going viral.

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:13.211
Someone posted a video
of a FedEx driver

00:10:13.211 --> 00:10:16.182
who didn't exactly deliver
their package with care.

00:10:16.182 --> 00:10:17.716
Watch this.

00:10:17.716 --> 00:10:20.953
-Woman in audience:
Oh, no.

00:10:20.953 --> 00:10:23.990
[ Laughter ]

00:10:28.127 --> 00:10:30.629
His boss called him and said,
"Just a little more practice,

00:10:30.629 --> 00:10:34.733
and you can do it without
slowing down the truck."

00:10:34.733 --> 00:10:36.235
Respect for that aim,
though, huh?

00:10:36.235 --> 00:10:37.770
-Yeah, that was good aim, man.

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:40.472
-Finally, a woman in Canada
was driving on a frozen river

00:10:40.472 --> 00:10:43.341
when the ice broke
and her car started to sink.

00:10:43.341 --> 00:10:46.612
And instead of panicking,
she took a selfie.

00:10:46.612 --> 00:10:48.047
Take a look.

00:10:50.248 --> 00:10:52.951
Don't worry. When the river
saw that it was a yellow Subaru,

00:10:52.951 --> 00:10:55.654
it spit the car right back up.

00:10:55.654 --> 00:10:57.856 line:0%
This afternoon, President Biden

00:10:57.856 --> 00:11:01.893 line:0%
held a press conference to
mark his first year in office.

00:11:01.893 --> 00:11:03.095
And this was smart.

00:11:03.095 --> 00:11:05.331
To make Biden look good,
they had the CDC Director

00:11:05.331 --> 00:11:10.269
go out first and open for him.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:10.269 --> 00:11:12.604
"Boo, yeah! okay."

00:11:12.604 --> 00:11:15.106
The press conference kicked off
at 4:00 p.m.

00:11:15.106 --> 00:11:16.474
You can tell it was really
important for Biden,

00:11:16.474 --> 00:11:18.444
because that's right in
the middle of dinner.

00:11:18.444 --> 00:11:20.112
[ Laughter ]

00:11:20.112 --> 00:11:22.814
"4:00 is when
I put my jammies on."

00:11:22.814 --> 00:11:24.750
Yeah, it was his first
formal press conference

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:27.119
at the White House
since March of last year.

00:11:27.119 --> 00:11:29.889
In Biden's defense, that one
just wrapped up a few days ago.

00:11:29.889 --> 00:11:31.190
[ Laughter ]

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:33.492
"I had an old friend named
Three-Toed Larry."

00:11:33.492 --> 00:11:37.663
[ Laughter ]

00:11:37.663 --> 00:11:40.499
"He had a big toe, a middle toe,
and another big toe."

00:11:40.499 --> 00:11:41.934
[ Laughter ]

00:11:41.934 --> 00:11:43.935
In his speech, Biden said
that we're in a better place

00:11:43.935 --> 00:11:46.171
with COVID
than we've been before.

00:11:46.171 --> 00:11:48.274
Then a reporter sneezed,
and everyone hit the floor.

00:11:48.274 --> 00:11:50.876
[ Laughter ]

00:11:50.876 --> 00:11:53.945
Biden also said, "Should we have
done more testing earlier?

00:11:53.945 --> 00:11:57.049
Yes, but we're doing more now."

00:11:57.049 --> 00:12:00.085
And he spent the next hour
asking himself questions until

00:12:00.085 --> 00:12:02.287
the press conference was over.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:02.287 --> 00:12:04.390
"Is the economy rebounding?
Yeah.

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:06.825
Did I see the new 'Spider-Man'?
No.

00:12:06.825 --> 00:12:09.628
Do I like superhero movies?
Yeah."

00:12:09.628 --> 00:12:10.930
But here's some good news.

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:14.032
Madame Tussauds just unveiled
their new figure

00:12:14.032 --> 00:12:16.768
of President Biden.
Take a look at this.

00:12:16.768 --> 00:12:18.204
[ Audience oohs ]

00:12:18.204 --> 00:12:21.240
Weirdly enough, that wax statue
has a 60% approval rating.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:23.542
-Really?
[ Laughter ]

00:12:23.542 --> 00:12:26.278
-Some more news, I saw that
the January 6th committee

00:12:26.278 --> 00:12:28.914
just issued subpoenas
to a few more of Trump's

00:12:28.914 --> 00:12:32.851 line:0%
former associates, including
his old lawyer, Rudy Giuliani.

00:12:32.851 --> 00:12:34.452 line:0%
You could tell Rudy
is not a very good lawyer,

00:12:34.452 --> 00:12:36.054
because the first thing
he did he was google,

00:12:36.054 --> 00:12:38.790
"What is a subpoena?"
[ Laughter ]

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:41.593
Rudy said he'd only comply
if his lawyer was present.

00:12:41.593 --> 00:12:43.362
Then he put a sock over his hand
and said,

00:12:43.362 --> 00:12:48.200
"I'm Mr. Giuliani's counsel."
[ Laughter ]

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.469
Meanwhile, if you google
Giuliani's subpoena,

00:12:50.469 --> 00:12:52.004
they show you a clip
from the "Borat" movie.

00:12:52.004 --> 00:12:56.108
[ Laughter ]

00:12:56.108 --> 00:12:58.777
-Come on.
-Some TV news.

00:12:58.777 --> 00:13:01.046
PBS just announced
that "Arthur,"

00:13:01.046 --> 00:13:03.348 line:0%
the longest-running animated
kids show in history,

00:13:03.348 --> 00:13:05.784 line:0%
will end next month
with a four --

00:13:05.784 --> 00:13:09.088 line:0%
[ Audience "aws" ]
...with a four-part finale

00:13:09.088 --> 00:13:12.558 line:0%
that shows the characters
as grown-ups.

00:13:12.558 --> 00:13:14.426
Yeah, aardvarks only live about
20 years,

00:13:14.426 --> 00:13:16.895
so this could get kind of heavy.
[ Laughter ]

00:13:16.895 --> 00:13:19.231
Here's Arthur as a kid.

00:13:19.231 --> 00:13:20.365
Yeah.

00:13:20.365 --> 00:13:22.500
And here he is as grown-up.
[ Laughter ]

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:24.903
Yeah, it's interesting.
So this is going to be cute.

00:13:24.903 --> 00:13:26.839
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:33.378 --> 00:13:35.947
Well, listen to this.
The CEO of Airbnb said that

00:13:35.947 --> 00:13:39.151 line:0%
he's going to permanently live
in Airbnb properties

00:13:39.151 --> 00:13:42.154 line:0%
and move to a new one
every two weeks.

00:13:42.154 --> 00:13:45.090
Yeah. The CEO of Motel 6 heard
this idea and was like,

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:48.760
"Do not expect that from me."
[ Laughter ]

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:51.730 line:0%
And finally, I read that Peloton
is reportedly considering

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:54.699 line:0%
scaling back
and closing some stores.

00:13:54.699 --> 00:13:56.034
We're three weeks into January.

00:13:56.034 --> 00:13:59.304
I didn't expect my bike
to be the one giving up.

00:13:59.304 --> 00:14:04.042 line:0%
Today marks one full year
in office for President Biden.

00:14:04.042 --> 00:14:06.511
It's been a challenging year.
When asked what he's learned,

00:14:06.511 --> 00:14:08.246
Biden said,
"Being vice president

00:14:08.246 --> 00:14:09.748
was a hell of a lot more fun."

00:14:09.748 --> 00:14:11.749
[ Laughter ]

00:14:11.749 --> 00:14:14.887
A year ago, Biden pledged
to address COVID, the economy,

00:14:14.887 --> 00:14:17.322
climate change,
and racial injustice.

00:14:17.322 --> 00:14:20.192
And good news -- after 12 months
of tireless effort,

00:14:20.192 --> 00:14:22.361
we're all getting
three free masks.

00:14:22.361 --> 00:14:24.262
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:14:24.262 --> 00:14:28.200
That's right.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:31.203
[ Laughter ]

00:14:31.203 --> 00:14:33.672
This is nice.
Biden's inaugural committee

00:14:33.672 --> 00:14:35.740
marked his anniversary
by releasing a video

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:39.478 line:0%
touting America's recovery,
narrated by Tom Hanks.

00:14:39.478 --> 00:14:41.913
Hanks wasn't the first choice,
but staffers had to explain

00:14:41.913 --> 00:14:44.316
to Biden that Gary Cooper
died 60 years ago.

00:14:44.316 --> 00:14:46.451
[ Laughter ]

00:14:46.451 --> 00:14:48.920
Meanwhile, yesterday, in his
two-hour press conference,

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:51.256
Biden --
two-hour press conference?

00:14:51.256 --> 00:14:53.459
[ Laughter ]
Biden covered a lot

00:14:53.459 --> 00:14:55.260
and said the U.S.
might not do anything

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:58.730 line:0%
if Russia's invasion of Ukraine
is only minor.

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:00.432 line:0%
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:15:00.432 --> 00:15:02.968 line:0%
One of his few slip-ups.
And it's a big deal,

00:15:02.968 --> 00:15:05.437 line:0%
'cause at Biden's age, any slip
could be a catastrophe.

00:15:05.437 --> 00:15:08.240
You know...
[ Laughter ]

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:11.076
What is a minor invasion?
[ Laughter ]

00:15:11.076 --> 00:15:12.711
A soldier sticks one foot
in Ukraine?

00:15:12.711 --> 00:15:16.715
He's like, "Just kidding!"
[ Laughter ]

00:15:16.715 --> 00:15:18.717
Well, today, Biden tried
to clear things up by saying

00:15:18.717 --> 00:15:21.053
any Russian invasion
would be met

00:15:21.053 --> 00:15:22.554
with severe economic response.

00:15:22.554 --> 00:15:24.189
Biden was like,
"Try me, tough guy,

00:15:24.189 --> 00:15:26.191
and I'll turn your economy
into ours."

00:15:26.191 --> 00:15:30.429
[ Laughter ]

00:15:30.429 --> 00:15:33.965
Yep, over time, Biden will hit
Putin with economic penalties.

00:15:33.965 --> 00:15:37.202
In other words, Biden is using
the same strategy as Netflix.

00:15:37.202 --> 00:15:38.870
[ Laughter ]

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:40.905
"It's only another dollar.

00:15:40.905 --> 00:15:43.475
Can't stop now."
[ Laughter ]

00:15:43.475 --> 00:15:45.077
During the press conference,
Biden also said

00:15:45.077 --> 00:15:48.880
that Kamala Harris would be his
running mate again in 2024.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:50.215
Then he mentioned
they're already working

00:15:50.215 --> 00:15:52.951
on potential campaign slogans
for their re-election.

00:15:52.951 --> 00:15:54.820
Take a look at these.
First up, there's...

00:15:57.956 --> 00:16:02.861
[ Laughter ]

00:16:02.861 --> 00:16:04.563
Next, they have...

00:16:07.533 --> 00:16:09.034 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:16:09.034 --> 00:16:10.402
And, finally, there's...

00:16:15.173 --> 00:16:16.575
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:16:16.575 --> 00:16:18.477
Pretty good.

00:16:20.979 --> 00:16:23.115
Some business news --
today Amazon announced

00:16:23.115 --> 00:16:24.717 line:0%
that this year,
it's opening its own

00:16:24.717 --> 00:16:27.752 line:0%
clothing store,
called Amazon Style.

00:16:27.752 --> 00:16:30.222
Though I'm not sure
Amazon Style is the best option

00:16:30.222 --> 00:16:32.057
when your founder
dresses like this.

00:16:32.057 --> 00:16:34.826
But I don't know. Maybe I'm...
[ Laughter ]

00:16:34.826 --> 00:16:36.861
That's right.
Amazon is focusing on clothing.

00:16:36.861 --> 00:16:38.597
Even crazier,
Abercrombie &amp; Fitch

00:16:38.597 --> 00:16:40.465
is going to start
launching people into space.

00:16:40.465 --> 00:16:42.634
[ Laughter ]
Isn't that...

00:16:42.634 --> 00:16:44.502
Well, this is fun.
I saw that Queen Elizabeth

00:16:44.502 --> 00:16:46.972 line:0%
is getting into
the condiment business.

00:16:46.972 --> 00:16:48.139 line:0%
That's right.
She's releasing her own

00:16:48.139 --> 00:16:51.043 line:0%
Royal Estate tomato sauce.

00:16:51.043 --> 00:16:53.078
Yeah, the Queen says
tomato sauce is just like

00:16:53.078 --> 00:16:54.680
her mother's servant
used to make.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.615
[ Laughter ]

00:17:00.452 --> 00:17:02.154
Did you guys see this?
Last week, Prince Andrew

00:17:02.154 --> 00:17:03.922
was stripped
of his royal status,

00:17:03.922 --> 00:17:06.425 line:0%
and now his official Twitter
and YouTube accounts

00:17:06.425 --> 00:17:08.293 line:0%
have been deleted.

00:17:08.293 --> 00:17:10.128
The Queen was like,
"No Twitter, no YouTube.

00:17:10.128 --> 00:17:11.463
Now go to your castle."

00:17:11.463 --> 00:17:14.533
[ Laughter ]

00:17:14.533 --> 00:17:18.670 line:0%
I saw that the CEO of crypto.com
just confirmed that it suffered

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:22.007 line:0%
a security breach, and hundreds
of accounts were hacked.

00:17:22.007 --> 00:17:23.408
That's terrible.

00:17:23.408 --> 00:17:25.911
I mean, if you can't trust
a website called crypto.com...

00:17:25.911 --> 00:17:30.148
[ Laughter ]

00:17:30.148 --> 00:17:32.584
Hey, I heard that police
in Canada are looking for a man

00:17:32.584 --> 00:17:35.420
who allegedly stole
an $8,000 guitar

00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:37.222
by hiding it in his pants.

00:17:37.222 --> 00:17:41.559
[ Laughter ]

00:17:41.559 --> 00:17:45.097
The first giveaway?
Guitar-shaped pants.

00:17:45.097 --> 00:17:47.499
[ Laughter ]

00:17:47.499 --> 00:17:49.734
When he was approached
by security, he was like,

00:17:49.734 --> 00:17:52.037
"Oh, I walked in with
this guitar in my pants."

00:17:52.037 --> 00:17:53.205
[ Laughter ]

00:17:53.205 --> 00:17:54.606
The guy was easy to spot.
He was the one

00:17:54.606 --> 00:17:56.307
walking away
from the store like...

00:17:56.307 --> 00:17:58.142
[ Guitar strumming ]

00:17:58.142 --> 00:18:00.445
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:18:00.445 --> 00:18:04.416
[ Strumming continues ]

00:18:04.416 --> 00:18:08.353
[ Laughter ]

00:18:08.353 --> 00:18:11.122
Finally, a home listing
in Wisconsin has gone viral

00:18:11.122 --> 00:18:13.958
because of the house's
unusual bathroom setup.

00:18:13.958 --> 00:18:15.894
Take a look at this. It's real.

00:18:15.894 --> 00:18:18.530
-Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:19.931
-It's weird when you knock
on the door, and three people

00:18:19.931 --> 00:18:22.567
are like, "Occupied!"
[ Laughter ]

00:18:22.567 --> 00:18:24.335
♪ Occupied ♪
-♪ Occupied ♪

00:18:24.335 --> 00:18:26.404
-♪ Occupied ♪
-♪ Occupied ♪

00:18:26.404 --> 00:18:28.473
-♪ Occupied ♪

00:18:28.473 --> 00:18:31.242
-Today the White House launched
a new phone line

00:18:31.242 --> 00:18:35.214
that Americans can call
to order their free COVID tests.

00:18:35.214 --> 00:18:36.948
Yeah, which means
100 million Americans

00:18:36.948 --> 00:18:39.117
spent the day screaming,
"Representative!

00:18:39.117 --> 00:18:42.320
[ Laughter and applause ]
Representative!

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:44.322
Human!"

00:18:44.322 --> 00:18:48.060
Yep, the phone line is open
from 8:00 a.m. to midnight.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:50.729
Somehow, the QVC phone lines
are open 24 hours a day,

00:18:50.729 --> 00:18:52.297
but the COVID hotline isn't.

00:18:52.297 --> 00:18:54.332
[ Laughter ]

00:18:54.332 --> 00:18:57.069
Meanwhile, we're a couple weeks
from the Winter Olympics

00:18:57.069 --> 00:18:58.436
and, due to COVID concerns,

00:18:58.436 --> 00:19:00.439
China is limiting
the torch relay

00:19:00.439 --> 00:19:02.774
to just three days.
[ Laughter ]

00:19:02.774 --> 00:19:05.110
And this is smart --
to maintain social distancing,

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:07.279
the runners will just throw
the torch to each other.

00:19:07.279 --> 00:19:09.981
[ Laughter ]

00:19:09.981 --> 00:19:11.349
Yep, thanks to COVID,
the Olympics

00:19:11.349 --> 00:19:12.784
are going to look
a little different.

00:19:12.784 --> 00:19:14.552 line:0%
I saw that NBC decided
not to send

00:19:14.552 --> 00:19:16.221 line:0%
its announcers to Beijing,

00:19:16.221 --> 00:19:18.323 line:0%
and, instead, they'll call
the games from Connecticut.

00:19:18.323 --> 00:19:20.658 line:0%
-[ Laughter ]
-Yeah!

00:19:20.658 --> 00:19:24.262
That's right. Connecticut,
instead of the Olympics.

00:19:24.262 --> 00:19:25.730
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:27.398
But on the bright side,
there'll be the same amount

00:19:27.398 --> 00:19:29.333
of people wearing Ralph Lauren
in both places.

00:19:29.333 --> 00:19:31.770
-[ Laughter and applause ]
-Oh.

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:33.504
-Announcers are upset
because there's nothing like

00:19:33.504 --> 00:19:34.906
being there in person

00:19:34.906 --> 00:19:37.142
to experience these
electrifying moments.

00:19:38.644 --> 00:19:40.679 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:19:42.447 --> 00:19:43.782
Wow.

00:19:43.782 --> 00:19:45.783
[ Laughter ]

00:19:45.783 --> 00:19:47.652
Well, this made me laugh --
Last night,

00:19:47.652 --> 00:19:50.121
Trump called in to "Hannity,"
and at one point,

00:19:50.121 --> 00:19:52.858
Hannity used a phrase
with the word "wall" in it,

00:19:52.858 --> 00:19:56.194
which immediately sent Trump
into his own world.

00:19:56.194 --> 00:19:57.295
Listen to this.

00:19:57.295 --> 00:19:59.163 line:0%
-So, you know,

00:19:59.163 --> 00:20:00.765 line:0%
you keep banging your head
against the wall,

00:20:00.765 --> 00:20:03.235 line:0%
why would you expect
a different result?

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:08.473 line:0%
-So, we would've had the wall
completed in three weeks.

00:20:08.473 --> 00:20:10.375 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]
It was largely completed.

00:20:10.375 --> 00:20:12.644
-No.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:20:12.644 --> 00:20:15.880
No, no, not -- Trump's
like a Golden Retriever.

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:17.515
A few key words
make him go wild.

00:20:17.515 --> 00:20:19.484
Like, "Wall, wall?
[ Panting ]

00:20:19.484 --> 00:20:20.752
Who said wall?
Who said wall?"

00:20:20.752 --> 00:20:22.620
[ Laughter ]

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:23.889
Some entertainment news --

00:20:23.889 --> 00:20:26.691 line:0%
the upcoming "Batman" movie
staring Robert Pattinson

00:20:26.691 --> 00:20:29.294 line:0%
will be one of the longest
superhero movies ever,

00:20:29.294 --> 00:20:31.763 line:0%
with a run time
of almost three hours.

00:20:31.763 --> 00:20:33.331
[ Audience ohs ]
Americans were like,

00:20:33.331 --> 00:20:35.634
"I'm not going to sit
through a three-hour movie..."

00:20:35.634 --> 00:20:37.836
and then settled in
for 14 hours of football.

00:20:37.836 --> 00:20:40.271
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:20:40.271 --> 00:20:42.040
That's right, three hours,
and there are plans

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:44.175
to extend the film
into a fourth hour,

00:20:44.175 --> 00:20:45.410
hosted by Hoda &amp; Jenna.

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:47.879
[ Laughter and applause ]
That's great.

00:20:47.879 --> 00:20:48.947
That's a good idea.

00:20:48.947 --> 00:20:51.015
In hindsight,
they probably didn't need

00:20:51.015 --> 00:20:53.085
20 minutes of Alfred
ironing the Batsuit.

00:20:53.085 --> 00:20:54.486
[ Laughter ]

00:20:54.486 --> 00:20:57.422
[As Michael Caine] "Your cape's
almost ready, Mr. Wayne."

00:20:57.422 --> 00:21:00.091
[ Laughter ]

00:21:00.091 --> 00:21:01.893
[ Applause ]
Speaking of movies....

00:21:01.893 --> 00:21:03.261
-Come on.

00:21:03.261 --> 00:21:04.662
[ Laughter ]

00:21:04.662 --> 00:21:06.431
-Speaking of movies,
the State of New York --

00:21:06.431 --> 00:21:07.933 line:0%
Did you see this?
They just announced

00:21:07.933 --> 00:21:10.268 line:0%
that movie theaters
can now sell alcohol.

00:21:10.268 --> 00:21:12.270 line:0%
-Ooh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:21:12.270 --> 00:21:14.005 line:0%
-No, no, no, no.

00:21:14.005 --> 00:21:16.875
No, no, I don't think
that's a good idea at all.

00:21:16.875 --> 00:21:18.643
[ Laughter ]
No. You know the annoying guy

00:21:18.643 --> 00:21:19.845
who yells stuff at the screen?

00:21:19.845 --> 00:21:21.779
Imagine him after eight beers,
you know?

00:21:21.779 --> 00:21:23.448
Seriously,
by the end of "Batman,"

00:21:23.448 --> 00:21:24.982
it's going to be like
"Royal Rumble."

00:21:24.982 --> 00:21:27.151
[ Laughter ]
It's like --

00:21:27.151 --> 00:21:29.321
Well, it's been a tough week
for Netflix.

00:21:29.321 --> 00:21:31.255
After admitting that all
the streaming competition

00:21:31.255 --> 00:21:33.191
has slowed growth,
their stock plummeted

00:21:33.191 --> 00:21:35.494
and they had their worst day
in years.

00:21:35.494 --> 00:21:37.061
Yeah, at the board meeting,
someone was like,

00:21:37.061 --> 00:21:39.898
"I don't know. Maybe 94 shows
about cakes is too much?"

00:21:39.898 --> 00:21:42.234
[ Laughter ]

00:21:42.234 --> 00:21:44.068
But don't worry.
Netflix isn't going anywhere.

00:21:44.068 --> 00:21:45.603
Mostly because
"Disney+ and chill"

00:21:45.603 --> 00:21:47.105
doesn't quite have
the same ring to it.

00:21:47.105 --> 00:21:48.340
[ Laughter ]

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:50.609 line:0%
And, finally, an underwear brand
called Parade

00:21:50.609 --> 00:21:52.043 line:0%
has a new recycling program

00:21:52.043 --> 00:21:54.579 line:0%
that turns their customers'
old underwear

00:21:54.579 --> 00:21:56.147 line:0%
into furniture and bedding.

00:21:56.147 --> 00:21:59.183 line:0%
[ Audience groans ]

00:21:59.183 --> 00:22:01.887
Even Greta Thunberg was like,
"Hell no!"

